{"id": "src:mimamsa-sutra", "title": "Mīmāṃsā Sūtra", "title_original": "मीमांसा सूत्र", "language": ["Sanskrit"], "script": ["Devanāgarī"], "family": "vedic", "lineages": ["lin:mimamsa", "lin:bhatta-mimamsa", "lin:prabhakara-mimamsa"], "authors": [{"teacher": "tch:jaimini", "role": "author", "attribution": "traditional"}], "alt_titles": ["Pūrvamīmāṃsāsūtra", "Jaiminisūtra", "Dvādaśalakṣaṇī", "Karmamīmāṃsāsūtra"], "genre": "sūtra", "attribution": {"tradition": "Jaimini, pupil of Vyāsa-Bādarāyaṇa", "scholarly": "attributed to Jaimini; the text cites earlier teachers (Bādari, Bādarāyaṇa, Aitiśāyana, Ātreya, Kārṣṇājini, Āśmarathya, Ālekhana, Lābukāyana, Kāmukāyana) and was probably compiled over time", "confidence": "moderate"}, "dating": {"tradition": {"text": "end of the Dvāpara age (the tradition's account)", "from": null, "to": null}, "scholarly": {"text": "c. 3rd c. BCE – 1st c. CE (estimates vary widely)", "from": -300, "to": 100}, "confidence": "low"}, "structure": {"description": "12 adhyāyas; adhyāyas 3, 6 and 10 have eight pādas, the rest four (60 pādas); c. 2,700 sūtras (one digital edition yields c. 2,720; counts vary by edition); about a thousand topics (adhikaraṇas)", "chapters": 12}, "key_teachings": ["tea:mimamsa-sutra:1.1.1", "tea:mimamsa-sutra:1.1.2", "tea:mimamsa-sutra:1.1.4", "tea:mimamsa-sutra:1.1.5", "tea:mimamsa-sutra:1.1.18", "tea:mimamsa-sutra:1.2.7", "tea:mimamsa-sutra:2.1.5", "tea:mimamsa-sutra:3.3.14", "tea:mimamsa-sutra:9.1.9"], "editions": [{"kind": "original", "name": "Mīmāṃsāsūtrāṇi, ebhāratī-sampat digital text (Rashtriya Sanskrit Vidyapeetha, Tirupati)", "licence": "unknown", "url": "https://www.ebharatisampat.in/read_chapter.php?bookid=NjMyOTA1NzgwODMyMzUy"}, {"kind": "original", "name": "sūtras embedded in the GRETIL Śābarabhāṣya (adhy. 1–7)", "licence": "GRETIL terms", "url": "http://gretil.sub.uni-goettingen.de/gretil/1_sanskr/6_sastra/3_phil/mimamsa/msbh1-7u.htm"}], "availability": "digitized-original", "notes": "Sūtra numbers used in this unit were checked against the two local digital editions named in editions; where they differ only in punctuation, the GRETIL wording is quoted.", "summary": "Jaimini's aphorisms on dharma known from Vedic injunction, in twelve adhyāyas (sixty pādas): (1) means of knowing dharma, (2) distinction of rites, (3) subsidiarity, (4) what prompts performance, (5) sequence, (6) eligibility, (7–8) general and specific transfer, (9) modification, (10) cancellation, (11) single performance for several, (12) incidental benefit. Its first pāda (the tarkapāda) grounds the authority of the authorless, eternal Veda.", "coverage": ["A5"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "src:sankarsa-kanda", "title": "Saṅkarṣa-kāṇḍa", "title_original": "सङ्कर्ष-काण्ड", "language": ["Sanskrit"], "script": ["Devanāgarī"], "family": "vedic", "lineages": ["lin:mimamsa"], "authors": [{"teacher": "tch:jaimini", "role": "author", "attribution": "disputed"}], "alt_titles": ["Saṃkarṣa-kāṇḍa", "Devatā-kāṇḍa", "Saṅkarṣaṇa-kāṇḍa"], "genre": "sūtra", "attribution": {"tradition": "Jaimini (Vṛttikāra tradition preserved by Rāmānuja)", "scholarly": "authorship disputed; some modern accounts connect it with Kāśakṛtsna", "confidence": "low"}, "structure": {"description": "4 adhyāyas", "chapters": 4}, "availability": "unknown", "notes": "The name 'Devatā-kāṇḍa' and the connection with deities are the tradition's; I could not check the extant state of the sūtras here. Commentary: Devasvāmin's bhāṣya (src:sankarsa-kanda-bhasya).", "summary": "A four-adhyāya supplement to the twelve adhyāyas of the Mīmāṃsā Sūtra, also called Devatā-kāṇḍa. The Vṛttikāra cited by Rāmānuja speaks of Jaimini's teaching in sixteen chapters (ṣoḍaśalakṣaṇa), i.e. the twelve plus these four, joined to the Śārīraka (Brahma Sūtra).", "coverage": ["A5"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "src:upavarsa-vrtti", "title": "Upavarṣa's vṛtti (lost)", "title_original": "उपवर्षऽस् वृत्ति", "language": ["Sanskrit"], "script": ["Devanāgarī"], "family": "vedic", "lineages": ["lin:mimamsa"], "authors": [{"teacher": "tch:upavarsa", "role": "commentator", "attribution": "traditional"}], "commentary_on": "src:mimamsa-sutra", "genre": "vṛtti", "availability": "lost", "notes": "Title is descriptive; no original title survives. Evidence: Śabara on MS 1.1.5; Śaṅkara, BSBh 3.3.53.", "summary": "A lost commentary by the 'revered Upavarṣa', cited by Śabara for the view that the word 'gauḥ' is just the letters g, au and ḥ; Śaṅkara reports that Upavarṣa, in the first (Pūrva Mīmāṃsā) treatise, deferred the proof of the self to the Śārīraka, implying he commented on both Mīmāṃsās.", "coverage": ["A5"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "src:bhavadasa-vrtti", "title": "Bhavadāsa's vṛtti (lost)", "title_original": "भवदासऽस् वृत्ति", "language": ["Sanskrit"], "script": ["Devanāgarī"], "family": "vedic", "lineages": ["lin:mimamsa"], "authors": [{"teacher": "tch:bhavadasa", "role": "commentator", "attribution": "accepted"}], "commentary_on": "src:mimamsa-sutra", "genre": "vṛtti", "availability": "lost", "summary": "A lost commentary on the Mīmāṃsā Sūtra by Bhavadāsa, mentioned by Kumārila (ŚV pratijñā 63) and, according to the Nyāyaratnākara, notable for dividing MS 1.1.4 into two sūtras.", "coverage": ["A5"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "src:sabara-bhasya", "title": "Śābarabhāṣya", "title_original": "शाबरभाष्य", "language": ["Sanskrit"], "script": ["Devanāgarī"], "family": "vedic", "lineages": ["lin:mimamsa", "lin:bhatta-mimamsa", "lin:prabhakara-mimamsa"], "authors": [{"teacher": "tch:sabara", "role": "commentator", "attribution": "accepted"}], "commentary_on": "src:mimamsa-sutra", "alt_titles": ["Mīmāṃsābhāṣya", "Śabarabhāṣya"], "genre": "bhāṣya", "dating": {"scholarly": {"text": "c. 3rd–5th c. CE (estimates vary)", "from": 200, "to": 500}, "confidence": "low"}, "key_teachings": ["tea:sabara-bhasya:1.1.2", "tea:sabara-bhasya:1.1.5", "tea:sabara-bhasya:2.1.5", "tea:sabara-bhasya:9.1.9"], "editions": [{"kind": "original", "name": "GRETIL e-text, adhyāyas 1–7", "licence": "GRETIL terms", "url": "http://gretil.sub.uni-goettingen.de/gretil/1_sanskr/6_sastra/3_phil/mimamsa/msbh1-7u.htm"}, {"kind": "original", "name": "Mīmāṃsādarśana with Śābarabhāṣya, ed. Ratna Gopāla Bhaṭṭa (Benares, 1910), OCR e-text", "licence": "public domain (1910 print)"}], "availability": "digitized-original", "summary": "Śabara's commentary on the whole Mīmāṃsā Sūtra, the root text of all later Mīmāṃsā. On the tarkapāda it defines injunction (codanā) as the statement that impels to action and the sole means of knowing dharma; it preserves the Vṛttikāra's definitions of six means of knowledge, his refutation of idealist and 'empty' views and his proof of the self; it explains apūrva (on MS 2.1.5) and discusses heaven, eligibility and the status of deities.", "coverage": ["A5"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "src:slokavarttika", "title": "Ślokavārttika", "title_original": "श्लोकवार्त्तिक", "language": ["Sanskrit"], "script": ["Devanāgarī"], "family": "vedic", "lineages": ["lin:bhatta-mimamsa"], "authors": [{"teacher": "tch:kumarila", "role": "commentator", "attribution": "accepted"}], "commentary_on": "src:sabara-bhasya", "alt_titles": ["Mīmāṃsāślokavārttika"], "genre": "vārttika", "structure": {"description": "verse (c. 3,000+ verses) on MS 1.1.1–32, in named sections"}, "key_teachings": ["tea:slokavarttika:codana.47", "tea:slokavarttika:codana.117-118", "tea:slokavarttika:pratyaksa.112", "tea:slokavarttika:sambandhaksepaparihara.108-111", "tea:slokavarttika:vakya.342-343"], "editions": [{"kind": "original", "name": "with Pārthasārathi's Nyāyaratnākara, ebhāratī-sampat digital text", "licence": "unknown"}, {"kind": "original", "name": "with Sucarita's Kāśikā (parts 1 and 3), digital texts", "licence": "unknown"}], "availability": "digitized-original", "summary": "Kumārila's verse sub-commentary on Śabara's tarkapāda (MS 1.1), in sections such as Pratijñā, Codanā, Pratyakṣa, Nirālambanavāda, Śūnyavāda, Autpattika, Anumāna, Śabda, Upamāna, Arthāpatti, Abhāva, Citrākṣepaparihāra, Sambandhākṣepaparihāra, Sphoṭavāda, Ākṛtivāda, Apohavāda, Vanavāda, Ātmavāda, Śabdanityatādhikaraṇa and Vākyādhikaraṇa. It defends intrinsic validity, the authorless Veda and a realist epistemology against Buddhist and other opponents, rejects omniscience in matters of dharma and a creator, and sets out the Bhāṭṭa view of release.", "coverage": ["A5"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
